WEBVTT

00:08.370 --> 00:15.570
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:08.370 --> 00:15.570
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

00:15.610 --> 00:22.320
Setsunai hodo mune utsu kagirinai kibou

00:15.610 --> 00:22.320
This unbounded hope that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

00:23.120 --> 00:30.920
Hakanasa wo masu hibi wo
irodoru wa kisetsu no kaze

00:23.120 --> 00:30.920
The days pass by, becoming more fleeting,
colored by the season's wind

00:30.960 --> 00:35.630
Kioku no kakera ga sawagidashita yo

00:30.960 --> 00:35.630
The fragments of memory started running wild

00:36.230 --> 00:44.630
Arinomama wo mitomete
haruka tsumuida hikari ga

00:36.230 --> 00:44.630
One more time, I want to hold the
spindle of far off light close to my breast,

00:44.680 --> 00:52.310
Kieru mae ni mou ichido
kono mune ni dakishimete

00:44.680 --> 00:52.310
Before it disappears, before
I accept the way things are now

00:54.390 --> 01:01.590
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:54.390 --> 01:01.590
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

01:01.590 --> 01:08.730
Mirai wo egaku ao ni kono te wo nobashite

01:01.590 --> 01:08.730
Hold out this hand to the blue-painted future

01:08.900 --> 01:16.030
Kasokushiteku sekai yo douka
yasashii mama de ite

01:08.900 --> 01:16.030
The world accelerates, please let it stay this kind

01:16.140 --> 01:23.640
Setsunai hodo mune utsu afuredasu negai

01:16.140 --> 01:23.640
This overflowing wish that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

01:34.490 --> 01:38.360


01:41.660 --> 01:45.130
It looks like the fireworks show today
will go off without a hitch.

01:45.130 --> 01:46.460
You're looking forward to it...

01:48.870 --> 01:51.340
Right? Of course.

01:58.280 --> 01:59.580
It was then...

02:00.150 --> 02:04.520
Or rather, ever since the summer program,

02:04.520 --> 02:06.610
something had been worrying me.

02:08.760 --> 02:10.050
Ichika?

02:10.590 --> 02:13.080
What's the matter? Is something wrong?

02:13.530 --> 02:16.700
Manatsu, the power of this charm...

02:16.700 --> 02:18.390
The power of the Djinn...

02:20.900 --> 02:25.400
The power I've been receiving from the Djinn...

02:25.540 --> 02:29.140
You mean getting the Djinn's "vision," right?

02:29.140 --> 02:30.010
Yes.

02:30.710 --> 02:34.480
Is there some meaning behind it?

02:35.620 --> 02:36.620
Meaning?

02:36.620 --> 02:37.240
Yes.

02:39.350 --> 02:42.590
How should I know something like that?

02:43.030 --> 02:44.860
Yes, I guess you're right.

02:44.860 --> 02:48.090
It was your homework to begin with, after all.

02:53.970 --> 02:55.470
K-Kai!

02:55.470 --> 02:57.370
What's the matter? You feeling okay?

02:57.370 --> 02:58.740
I-I'm
sorry!

02:59.570 --> 03:01.480
To see something.

03:01.480 --> 03:04.970
Just being able to see something
doesn't mean you can solve it.

03:06.980 --> 03:12.390
At that time, I could not help
but feel unconvinced.

03:14.000 --> 03:18.500
The Flowering of Tears

03:22.660 --> 03:23.460
Kai...

03:24.930 --> 03:29.100
What does "seeing" mean?

03:29.100 --> 03:33.560
Is there some meaning behind the ability to see?

03:35.610 --> 03:38.480
It's true that seeing might be a simple thing.

03:39.180 --> 03:43.020
But they say that just by seeing something,
you can change it.

03:43.020 --> 03:44.750
Is that true?

03:45.150 --> 03:46.150
Yes.

03:46.150 --> 03:50.020
In the fields of particle physics
and quantum mechanics.

03:50.990 --> 03:53.760
You can't see in the pitch dark, yes?

03:53.760 --> 03:54.420
Right.

03:54.760 --> 03:58.900
Light can act both like a wave and a particle,

03:58.900 --> 04:01.900
and in order to see
you need that light to fall on things.

04:01.900 --> 04:06.370
But those things are also in the realm
of tiny elementary particles,

04:06.370 --> 04:10.070
so when the light hits the particles,
it causes them to move.

04:11.550 --> 04:15.140
Does something good come from "seeing"?

04:15.550 --> 04:18.590
Good or not, you are the "observer".

04:18.590 --> 04:20.560
Beauty is in your eye, so to speak.

04:21.660 --> 04:22.450
Right!

04:22.890 --> 04:25.530
You're going to the fireworks show, right?

04:25.530 --> 04:28.500
Then get this finished up before noon,
like you planned!

04:28.500 --> 04:30.430
Right! I'll do my best!

04:32.530 --> 04:34.470
Then, if you'll excuse me.

04:37.540 --> 04:40.980
I suppose saying that much
isn't against the rules.

04:48.680 --> 04:50.450
I knew it...

04:57.490 --> 04:59.820
Wow, you can put on your own yukata!

05:00.100 --> 05:04.000
Yes. My late grandmother taught me how.

05:04.000 --> 05:06.060
Man, I'm jealous...

05:09.670 --> 05:11.770
Why don't you try...

05:11.770 --> 05:14.210
Man, I'm jealous...

05:16.880 --> 05:18.950
There, all finished!

05:18.950 --> 05:22.350
Wow, it's so pretty!

05:22.950 --> 05:24.180
Does it look good on me?

05:25.690 --> 05:29.660
Oh, you let Manatsu borrow your yukata?

05:29.660 --> 05:32.680
Yes. But I'm at least wearing this.

05:32.990 --> 05:35.530
That's Grandma's obi clasp, yes?

05:35.530 --> 05:36.160
Right!

05:39.840 --> 05:41.670
We're heading out!

05:44.140 --> 05:45.540
Let's hurry, okay?

05:45.540 --> 05:48.340
We're going to be late meeting up.

05:48.340 --> 05:49.640
Hey, wait!

05:53.450 --> 05:56.020
Ichika, Manatsu, you're late!

05:56.020 --> 05:57.990
I'm sorry for being late!

05:57.990 --> 05:59.250
Sorry!

05:59.250 --> 06:01.150
Oh? Where's Keiko?

06:06.600 --> 06:07.720
Thank you.

06:09.560 --> 06:11.500
I'm late!

06:11.500 --> 06:13.400
No kidding, Keiko.

06:14.800 --> 06:17.840
Ichika, where's your yukata?

06:17.840 --> 06:20.910
Yes... I let Manatsu borrow it.

06:20.910 --> 06:23.210
I borrowed it from Ichika!

06:23.210 --> 06:24.940
I am pretending to be Ichika!

06:26.510 --> 06:27.410
...Ichika.

06:29.580 --> 06:31.950
Don't impersonate me!

06:35.190 --> 06:38.250
I don't look any good in a yukata.

06:38.690 --> 06:42.150
Japanese clothing doesn't
go with large breasts, yes.

06:43.730 --> 06:45.670
Must be nice, Keiko...

06:47.270 --> 06:50.070
I knew I should have worn a yukata...

06:50.070 --> 06:51.710
But it's still noon.

06:51.710 --> 06:54.140
It'll be evening soon.

06:55.040 --> 06:57.610
I'm gettin' a feeling like I'm ahead of the game!

06:57.610 --> 06:59.940
Although you don't have a boyfriend.

07:00.520 --> 07:01.820
Why, you...

07:01.820 --> 07:03.950
We can pick some up when we get there!

07:03.950 --> 07:05.150
Let's go!

07:05.150 --> 07:05.550
Roger!

07:05.550 --> 07:06.820
Roger!

07:07.990 --> 07:13.120
The beach!

07:14.530 --> 07:16.120
Hey, Manatsu!

07:24.110 --> 07:27.080
Manatsu's like a little child.

07:47.600 --> 07:50.600
Sorry, I know it's borrowed...

07:50.600 --> 07:52.730
No, don't worry about it.

07:53.030 --> 07:57.300
Anyway, we got ourselves a good spot.

07:57.770 --> 07:58.930
Takigawa?

08:01.680 --> 08:02.640
Nozomu?

08:03.650 --> 08:05.370
It is you, Takigawa!

08:05.710 --> 08:07.980
You went to an all-girls middle school, right?

08:07.980 --> 08:09.280
Long time no see.

08:30.670 --> 08:32.700
Hey there!

08:33.170 --> 08:35.540
Come to help out again?

08:35.840 --> 08:39.510
No! Today we are customers!

08:44.390 --> 08:46.250
A group date?

08:46.250 --> 08:47.880
Things are lookin' up, huh?

08:48.320 --> 08:50.360
Y-you big dummy!

08:50.360 --> 08:52.690
We were in the same class in elementary school!

08:52.690 --> 08:56.460
Sure, whatever. Table for seven, please!

08:56.460 --> 08:58.870
He is such an idiot!

08:58.870 --> 09:00.270
Oh, Satsuki...

09:00.570 --> 09:02.700
That's Takigawa's brother?

09:02.700 --> 09:04.670
Yes, he is.

09:04.670 --> 09:07.110
He's the same as always.

09:07.110 --> 09:09.600
I wish he'd grow up a little.

09:12.610 --> 09:14.840
Yes. Things are looking up.

09:17.790 --> 09:21.320
There are more part time workers
than the last time.

09:21.320 --> 09:22.690
Yeah!

09:22.690 --> 09:25.130
It looks like we won't have to help.

09:25.130 --> 09:28.800
Today is the fireworks show though...
It might be busy.

09:28.800 --> 09:31.500
If we're helping we won't get to
see the fireworks, duh.

09:31.500 --> 09:36.000
Good job gettin' us these cute girls, Nozomu!

09:36.770 --> 09:38.370
Don't be silly, Shigeru.

09:38.370 --> 09:40.610
She's just a friend from elementary school.

09:40.610 --> 09:42.480
No seriously, I appreciate it.

09:42.480 --> 09:47.110
Then that dog and Jiromon
have started to get along...

09:49.920 --> 09:52.950
What do "star mine" fireworks mean, I wonder?

09:52.950 --> 09:55.020
I bet you know, Michiru.

09:55.020 --> 09:57.230
I know what "star" means in English,

09:57.230 --> 09:59.520
but what does "mine" mean?

10:00.800 --> 10:01.920
Welcome home.

10:02.360 --> 10:03.490
You were quite late.

10:03.800 --> 10:04.490
Yes.

10:05.000 --> 10:05.990
What's the matter?

10:09.040 --> 10:11.170
I saw her.

10:14.640 --> 10:15.910
Her?

10:15.910 --> 10:18.280
She was quite different than my impression...

10:18.810 --> 10:21.370
But there's no mistaking it.

10:22.880 --> 10:25.380
Saya is...

10:37.100 --> 10:39.230
Then let's go for a swim till it starts!

10:39.230 --> 10:40.400
Yes, let's.

10:44.870 --> 10:47.110
When does the fireworks show start?

10:47.110 --> 10:48.610
At night, right?

10:48.610 --> 10:50.310
Yes. It begins at 7.

10:52.650 --> 10:54.320
What are you lookin' at?

10:54.320 --> 10:56.150
N-nothing.

10:57.590 --> 10:58.750
There!

11:04.860 --> 11:07.120
Takigawa, huh?

11:09.460 --> 11:16.130
Why do I keep coming to the beach
when I can't go in the saltwater?

11:19.910 --> 11:21.930
It's almost closing time for swimming.

11:22.340 --> 11:25.110
Let's get out before the
changing rooms get too full.

11:25.110 --> 11:25.840
Yes, let's.

11:29.120 --> 11:31.550
Looks like we were too late.

11:31.550 --> 11:33.350
What'll we do?

11:33.350 --> 11:34.480
I don't know...

11:49.440 --> 11:52.370
Hey, can't people see you from above?

11:53.440 --> 11:56.110
Don't go yelling that!

11:56.110 --> 11:57.240
Sorry 'bout this!

12:06.350 --> 12:09.860
Satsuki... About that boy...

12:09.860 --> 12:12.120
Don't be silly! It's not...

12:13.260 --> 12:14.520
...like that, okay?

12:25.610 --> 12:26.870
It looks good on you.

12:27.540 --> 12:30.010
Thank you, Ichika!

12:30.410 --> 12:33.050
That's enough, we're finished!

12:33.050 --> 12:34.010
Okay!

12:41.620 --> 12:43.730
What are you looking at?

12:43.730 --> 12:45.690
We've got to change too, you know!

12:45.690 --> 12:46.920
R-right...

13:01.080 --> 13:02.630
You shouldn't stand.

13:03.810 --> 13:06.340
There are people behind us.

13:07.180 --> 13:10.650
There is still an hour until they begin.

13:10.650 --> 13:12.490
Yes...

13:12.490 --> 13:13.650
Then...

13:14.020 --> 13:15.220
Excuse me!

13:15.660 --> 13:17.220
Yes, coming!

13:19.530 --> 13:22.760
It looks like his place is really packed.

13:22.760 --> 13:24.730
Let's go to another shop.

13:24.730 --> 13:26.430
You're not finished yet?

13:26.730 --> 13:28.930
We're all thirsty, right?

13:29.840 --> 13:32.570
If you want to buy some juice,
we have to drop these off or...

13:32.570 --> 13:33.510
Yes, I agree.

13:33.510 --> 13:34.370
So do I.

13:36.310 --> 13:40.010
Damn it... Why am I the errand boy?

13:41.780 --> 13:44.320
Looks like we should each buy them separately.

13:44.320 --> 13:45.580
Yeah...

13:47.520 --> 13:48.510
Takigawa.

13:49.920 --> 13:51.790
I want to speak with you, alone.

13:52.460 --> 13:53.630
What?

13:53.630 --> 13:55.820
Meet me over there after you finish buying.

13:56.060 --> 13:58.060
What? But...

14:00.230 --> 14:02.540
Haven't they brought the drinks yet?

14:02.540 --> 14:04.470
Manatsu, you're such a little kid.

14:04.770 --> 14:07.170
But they really are taking a while.

14:07.180 --> 14:10.670
It always feels longer
when you are the one waiting.

14:18.920 --> 14:20.010
Keiko!

14:20.820 --> 14:21.950
Over here.

14:23.460 --> 14:26.450
Oh? Where's Satsuki?

14:35.340 --> 14:37.300
I think she went over this way.

14:44.150 --> 14:47.450
I hope Satsuki can get over
her hatred of men this way.

14:58.530 --> 14:59.960
Then, you see...

15:00.900 --> 15:02.450
Satsuki!

15:04.670 --> 15:06.570
You're late!

15:06.570 --> 15:09.270
Sorry, I got separated!

15:09.270 --> 15:11.310
Where's Nozomu and Keiko?

15:11.310 --> 15:12.410
They aren't back yet.

15:12.410 --> 15:14.070
Weren't you together?

15:15.480 --> 15:18.210
The fireworks will begin momentarily.

15:19.350 --> 15:21.750
Nozomu's totally doing this to me on purpose.

15:25.790 --> 15:29.260
Perhaps he's searching for you, Satsuki?

15:29.260 --> 15:30.850
Try calling them on your cellphone!

15:40.540 --> 15:42.660
That's Keiko's...

15:43.770 --> 15:45.830
I'll go look for them.

15:46.140 --> 15:47.170
Satsuki!

15:47.180 --> 15:50.110
Don't worry. You guys stay here.

15:58.090 --> 15:59.780
Oh, it's starting!

16:05.190 --> 16:07.250
Good luck, Satsuki!

16:13.100 --> 16:15.660
I'm going to look for them.

16:17.340 --> 16:18.910
Just let 'em be...

16:18.910 --> 16:20.210
I'm going too!

16:20.210 --> 16:21.370
Sheesh...

16:31.120 --> 16:33.120
Everywhere is full of people...

16:33.120 --> 16:35.590
This is the only place people can't see us.

16:36.990 --> 16:38.460
You're going to use it, right?

16:41.300 --> 16:46.500
I think using the Djinn's "vision"
is for a time like this, right?

16:48.440 --> 16:49.060
Yeah...

17:20.800 --> 17:24.700
Please, lend me your power.

17:24.710 --> 17:27.400
Please lend me your vision!

17:48.930 --> 17:50.690
Thank you!

18:05.110 --> 18:06.440
Satsuki...

18:19.230 --> 18:20.280
I love you...

18:24.500 --> 18:26.190
Keiko...

18:26.730 --> 18:27.900
Satsuki...

18:35.940 --> 18:40.900
The fifth, the spirit of flame... The Djinn, Pyra.

18:51.090 --> 18:55.060
Yup, no way I'd find them in this crowd!

18:55.060 --> 18:57.790
I'm sure the two of them
are watching from somewhere.

18:58.330 --> 18:59.730
Satsuki...

19:02.040 --> 19:05.940
It's okay. We're not children anymore.

19:05.940 --> 19:07.470
Let's go back.

19:08.580 --> 19:13.100
Michiru and the others... must be waiting.

19:14.480 --> 19:16.310
Satsuki...

19:31.330 --> 19:33.860
Ichika... Manatsu...

19:34.370 --> 19:35.600
Don't look!

19:36.070 --> 19:38.900
I don't want you to see me like this!

19:50.550 --> 19:54.290
Hey, isn't that Ichika and her friends?

19:54.290 --> 19:55.480
Yeah...

19:56.720 --> 19:57.820
Ichika!

20:01.100 --> 20:06.690
Ichika, don't tell anyone I was crying.

20:08.070 --> 20:10.300
What are you doing here?

20:10.300 --> 20:11.610
Uh, well...

20:11.610 --> 20:13.970
Wow, that was a big one!

20:13.970 --> 20:16.480
Ichika, did you just see that?

20:16.480 --> 20:17.470
Yes...

20:18.650 --> 20:26.820
In the end, I could only see.
I wasn't able to change anything...

20:27.350 --> 20:33.520
I wasn't able to help anyone at all that time.

20:45.770 --> 20:49.310
Well, I'd better get back.

20:49.310 --> 20:51.280
Tell Nozomu if you see him.

20:54.650 --> 20:55.770
Where's Nozomu?

20:56.280 --> 20:58.220
He went back toward the station.

20:58.220 --> 21:00.280
Why that jerk!

21:01.260 --> 21:02.220
I'm back.

21:05.160 --> 21:08.930
I'm sorry we got separated Satsuki...

21:09.330 --> 21:13.000
No. I think I was the one that got split up.

21:13.000 --> 21:16.300
But since we decided to gather here
before we went home...

21:16.300 --> 21:16.930
Ichika.

21:17.640 --> 21:18.610
Yes?

21:18.610 --> 21:21.010
Fix Keiko's yukata, would you?

21:21.580 --> 21:22.270
Okay.

21:23.010 --> 21:25.650
I borrowed the Djinn's vision,

21:25.650 --> 21:29.620
but back then I didn't notice
the other people watching me.

21:29.620 --> 21:31.320
But back then I didn't notice
the other people watching me.
I love yukatas, don't you?

21:31.320 --> 21:33.190
But back then I didn't notice
the other people watching me.

21:33.890 --> 21:37.520
Okay then, let's go, full steam ahead!

21:47.500 --> 21:50.470


21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
Hora kotoshi mo ame furu gogo
hakanai utakata no iro

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
See, this year the afternoon rain falls again
in the color of fleeting bubbles

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
Sora mo yasashiku mienai wa
datte hitori da mono

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
The sky doesn't look kind to me, after all,
I'm alone

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
Itazura na sadame ni kotoba mo denai wa

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
I have no more words for the tricks of fate

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Wakariaeta futari ni mou modorenai no?

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Can we never return to two
who understood each other?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

23:20.460 --> 23:20.490


23:20.490 --> 23:21.730


23:21.730 --> 23:27.230
On that day I came to realize that just as the
brittle, dry earth sucks up the rain in an instant,

23:27.240 --> 23:34.040
people's parched hearts never cease yearning
for the feelings of others.

23:34.940 --> 23:39.940
Next time on Uta~Kata:
The Flush of Damp Skin
